WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
(audience cheering)
- Welcome back, y'all.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.590
My next guest is one of
the bestselling authors

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.950
on the planet.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.900
Since her debut novel in 2012,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.570
she has sold over 40 million books

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.850
and redefined the fantasy genre.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.010
Her latest is "House of Flame and Shadow,"

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.680
the third book in her
"Crescent City" series.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.730
This is amazing, actually,

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.563
just check this out.

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:19.890
How many people actually showed up

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.620
to her midnight release party last week.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.450
It's like Taylor Swift went somewhere.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.380
Isn't it crazy?

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.760
Is that normal by the way?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.593
Like last night?

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.820
I mean, even "Vulture" wrote
something about you like,

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.070
you did this release and
like it just blew up.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.620
It literally was like Taylor
Swift was releasing an album,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.630
like all these people showed up.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:37.953
Is that normal?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.675
- Well-

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:40.740
- I guess you feel like
a tool answering that.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.573
- I don't know.
- Is it, yeah,

00:00:41.573 --> 00:00:42.828
I was like, "Wait,
that's a weird question."

00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:44.228
But, I mean, that's amazing, the impact.

00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:45.061
- You know what, you know what,

00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:47.010
you know, this was
actually my first event,

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.914
like in person event since COVID.

00:00:49.914 --> 00:00:50.917
- Oh my goodness.
- Yeah.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.170
So this was kinda like my first time

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.390
like back in the flesh.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.040
- Well, by the way, you're in demand.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:56.873
Look at that.

00:00:56.873 --> 00:00:57.706
Like, well that's, you're
doing, you're doing it right.

00:00:57.706 --> 00:00:59.490
- Oh my god, it was amazing.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.050
It was just amazing being out there

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.810
and like seeing the
readers face to face again

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.283
after so many years and.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.610
- And you've created this
world, like whichever series,

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.500
you know, they're addicted to or into,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.850
like you've created this whole world

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.080
that y'all are all a part of.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:13.913
That's really cool.

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:15.150
- Yeah, no, it's just, it's, I mean,

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.338
it still feels like a dream come true.

00:01:17.338 --> 00:01:20.460
Like I wanted to be a writer
since I was 16 years old.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.773
- That's amazing.
- Yeah.

